{"term": "kenarcu", "lang": "tr", "script": "latin", "romanization": null, "category": "sex_work_pornography", "subcategory": "street_prostitute", "concept": "street_prostitution", "is_novel_concept": false, "register": "slang_neutral", "crude": 60, "technical": 10, "recognition_pct_current": 45, "recognition_pct_peak": 45, "peak_year": null, "regional": null, "definition": "Colloquial Turkish term for a sex worker who solicits from the outskirts or peripheral roads of a city, typically approaching cars; derived from 'kenar' (edge, margin, roadside) with the agentive suffix '-cu'.", "english_term": "streetwalker", "english_translation_quality": "approximate", "notes": "The '-cu/-cü' agentive suffix marks someone whose work is associated with the 'kenar' (roadside/urban periphery); specifically implies car-side solicitation on peripheral urban roads rather than central street prostitution. Less widely known than 'sokak kadını'; possibly more common in certain regional dialects."}
